.TH geectl-changelog-generate 1  "geectl-changelog-generate 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-changelog\-generate \- Generate a skeleton `.changes` entry from the diff against the target (version line, patch and dependency lists, license lines) plus the upstream NEWS section for the new version, extracted from the source tarball. The output is a draft: what the diff cannot supply arrives as explicit `TODO` slots for a human to fill. `\-\-write` prepends the draft into the package\*(Aqs `.changes` file, and refuses an incomplete draft (V9 needs\-detail)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl changelog generate\fR [\fB\-\-target\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-target\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-author\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-message\fR] [\fB\-\-write\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIDIR\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate a skeleton `.changes` entry from the diff against the target (version line, patch and dependency lists, license lines) plus the upstream NEWS section for the new version, extracted from the source tarball. The output is a draft: what the diff cannot supply arrives as explicit `TODO` slots for a human to fill. `\-\-write` prepends the draft into the package\*(Aqs `.changes` file, and refuses an incomplete draft (V9 needs\-detail)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-project\fR \fI<TARGET_PROJECT>\fR
The target project to diff against
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-package\fR \fI<TARGET_PACKAGE>\fR
The target package to diff against
.TP
\fB\-\-author\fR \fI<AUTHOR>\fR
The author line for the entry header, in `Name <email>` form — exactly what a bare `changelog` invocation writes
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-message\fR \fI<MESSAGE>\fR
Custom message bullets for the entry, one bullet per `\-m`. Repeatable: `\-m "Fix the crash" \-m "Add the subcommand"`. A message may span lines — embedded newlines become indented continuation lines of that bullet, and a blank line inside a message is a paragraph break within it. A leading `\- `, `* ` or `+ ` marker is stripped, never double\-bulleted. The message is the human detail: it replaces the TODO summary slot, so `\-\-write` no longer refuses the draft for the missing message; other TODO slots still refuse
.TP
\fB\-\-write\fR
Prepend the draft into the package\*(Aqs `.changes` file instead of printing it. The whole file is normalized on write: trailing ASCII whitespace stripped, CRLF→LF, legacy encodings transcoded to UTF\-8, a BOM stripped. The write is atomic and refuses a symlink destination, an unreadable file, or bytes no known encoding decodes. A file decoded from a guessed single\-byte encoding is transcoded on the guess instead — a wrong guess cannot be detected — and the write warns about it, naming the encoding
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIDIR\fR] [default: .]
The package directory (default: the current directory)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
